INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (460009382302015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Basic Chemical Calculations”, how should Ideal Gas Law. NTP & STP be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Introduction”, how should Derived quantities be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Introduction”, how should power be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions”, how should Evaporation. Introduction to Recycle & By-pass operation. be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** The ideal gas equation PV=nRT relates pressure, volume, moles and absolute temperature under ideal-gas assumptions.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Basic Chemical Calculations; Definition of Atomic weight and Molecular wt.; Calculation of Molecular weight of various compounds; Introduction to Avogadro’s Number & Moles concept. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Basic Chemical Calculations. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Derived quantities is listed under “Introduction” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Introduction, Importance of process calculations, Dimensions and systems of units, Fundamental quantities, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Introduction; Importance of process calculations; Dimensions and systems of units; Fundamental quantities. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Introduction. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** power is listed under “Introduction” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Introduction, Importance of process calculations, Dimensions and systems of units, Fundamental quantities, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Introduction; Importance of process calculations; Dimensions and systems of units; Fundamental quantities. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Introduction. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Evaporation removes solvent as vapor to concentrate a solution; heat supply, boiling point elevation and product sensitivity matter.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions; Definition of Law of Conversation of Mass; Process flow diagram; significance of Material balance in chemical industry. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

