VALUES (460009382303015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”, how should Indian standards (IS) and codes be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”, how should ears be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”, how should ISO 14001 be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”, how should HAZAN and HAZOP be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** COD estimates chemically oxidizable matter in a water sample and is not identical to BOD.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE; Definition of Safety; Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries; Development of safety organization. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** COD estimates chemically oxidizable matter in a water sample and is not identical to BOD.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE; Definition of Safety; Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries; Development of safety organization. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** COD estimates chemically oxidizable matter in a water sample and is not identical to BOD.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE; Definition of Safety; Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries; Development of safety organization. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** HAZOP systematically examines deviations from design intent using guide words and records causes, consequences and safeguards.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Hazard Identification and control Techaniques; Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards; Classification of Chemical Hazards; occupational health hazards and control. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Hazard Identification and control Techaniques. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

