VALUES (4600093823030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply Definition of Safety in “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards in “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Ventilation and lighting in “Control of Chemical Hazards”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Definition of pollution and pollutant in “Types of pollution and pollutants”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Definition of Safety is covered in “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries, Development of safety organization, Indian standards (IS) and codes, International Standards like ISO 9001, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries, Development of safety organization, Indian standards (IS) and codes, International Standards like ISO 9001.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards is covered in “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Classification of Chemical Hazards, occupational health hazards and control, Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect, Hazard and Operatability study (HAZOP), give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Classification of Chemical Hazards, occupational health hazards and control, Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect, Hazard and Operatability study (HAZOP).\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Ventilation and lighting is covered in “Control of Chemical Hazards”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards, Thermal Hazards, Chemical burns and their effect, Colour codes and symbols for safety, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards, Thermal Hazards, Chemical burns and their effect, Colour codes and symbols for safety.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Definition of pollution and pollutant is covered in “Types of pollution and pollutants”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Sources of Pollution, Effect of pollution on Human health, Air pollution, Water pollution, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Sources of Pollution, Effect of pollution on Human health, Air pollution, Water pollution.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

