s with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Pressure Concept: Definitions of static head is listed under “Fluid Statics and its Applications” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Fluid Statics and its Applications, Introduction of Fluid static and dynamics, Nature of Fluid, Ideal fluid & Real fluid, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Fluid Statics and its Applications; Introduction of Fluid static and dynamics; Nature of Fluid; Ideal fluid & Real fluid. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Fluid Statics and its Applications. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Vacuum (negative pressure) is listed under “Fluid Statics and its Applications” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Fluid Statics and its Applications, Introduction of Fluid static and dynamics, Nature of Fluid, Ideal fluid & Real fluid, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Fluid Statics and its Applications; Introduction of Fluid static and dynamics; Nature of Fluid; Ideal fluid & Real fluid. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Fluid Statics and its Applications. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Mach- Number is listed under “Basic Equations of Fluid Flow” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Basic Equations of Fluid Flow, Continuity equation, Average velocity, Mass velocity, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Basic Equations of Fluid Flow; Continuity equation; Average velocity; Mass velocity. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Basic Equations of Fluid Flow. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

